er/id #uuid "9dd4d6cf-d2eb-5057-a61d-f4342bd71757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Singular" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358557} {:answer/id #uuid "8e97e7d3-20d5-5852-aa6f-0eca5b0181b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reduced" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358558} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d2431e-08b0-501c-a042-e5b786752943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Invertible" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358559} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba5b28f-3cd8-5a45-995d-d0537a54a620" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Transpose" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358560} {:answer/id #uuid "e1c7d9a5-a44f-5582-b459-db335110b74e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6d2431e-08b0-501c-a042-e5b786752943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Invertible" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358559} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a5e1be7-6263-52f9-9055-829d36ebcfa2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "891a0e2e-cbca-5e23-84ac-2045f86b17cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-142302" :question/problem "$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{ }\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is \"invertible\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358562 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "879514d5-e127-5485-ab41-d459f6b5f379" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Parts of the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15db2e53-e3a0-56fb-bd7b-1ab3aec1c118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358564} {:answer/id #uuid "6fa26364-583c-5c9b-90f6-39c139763c28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "det({A}^{n})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358565} {:answer/id #uuid "658b261a-79b0-5c7f-9446-18f0e0b3846a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}({A}^{n})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358566} {:answer/id #uuid "a097d858-2f1e-541a-adc3-1bbe0122b398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "det(I-{A}^{n})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358567} {:answer/id #uuid "d21d1e44-1a6b-5a6d-85c6-cb0c33bc1a90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}({A}^{-1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15db2e53-e3a0-56fb-bd7b-1ab3aec1c118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358564} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb8282ff-2538-5886-a053-3357678bd2ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4ba2574-bff5-58c4-8806-875f992caa79" :question/math-academy-id "q-142357" :question/problem "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & ={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\text{Col}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358569 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb2ca3e6-3016-52bb-93ac-cf5addf3c8c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358571} {:answer/id #uuid "f4bbb2b9-d256-5c64-bd14-99273892263f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358572} {:answer/id #uuid "f76a542b-1405-5ac5-bbf2-dcf467246fec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358573} {:answer/id #uuid "000fec77-bea3-5b1e-b69c-342c6527bcc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358574} {:answer/id #uuid "461740ba-304c-580c-b0bc-3441fd162292" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "000fec77-bea3-5b1e-b69c-342c6527bcc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358574} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b6b2619-8d04-5edb-8689-da6db3e8af02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9de3bb13-65d5-5b1c-b866-679fe9bf3723" :question/math-academy-id "q-142358" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}?\n$$\n\n- $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$\n- $A$ is  invertible\n- $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358576 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a9d9a60-34d8-5050-bf02-51f9eb9c1493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358578} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9a564f-ae9a-57e3-8171-563ca3cdf256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358579} {:answer/id #uuid "f4276993-4c56-519f-b025-2850b8913d9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358580} {:answer/id #uuid "aabbc51c-60f1-5bed-b20c-fec002483c2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358581} {:answer/id #uuid "3db264c1-f171-57eb-b0ed-3dd6b9081b80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4276993-4c56-519f-b025-2850b8913d9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358580} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1bfa085-a8c7-507c-af46-3f860c19c809" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7804590c-275e-53bf-9345-63a0af840940" :question/math-academy-id "q-142474" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}?\n$$\n\n- $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$\n- $A$ is invertible\n- $\\text{rank}(A)<4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ or equivalently $\\text{rank}(A)<4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "838922a0-4f80-5a2d-a815-ffe5dad39a64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358585} {:answer/id #uuid "0008a54d-7378-566c-a10e-1a773a81a6f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358586} {:answer/id #uuid "9029d208-384f-5e55-ace6-ed268ed3b780" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358587} {:answer/id #uuid "2f39ca14-fe89-5866-884a-29c5a6d1cba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358588} {:answer/id #uuid "a00fb4f8-dfe8-5084-9541-74d079a8bf3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0008a54d-7378-566c-a10e-1a773a81a6f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358586} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0bfb7f-a500-50cb-b054-49ebea8f394c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "498bc0be-a243-5afb-9437-0b2b1ad99954" :question/math-academy-id "q-142475" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n- $A$ is invertible\n- $\\text{rank}(A)<n$\n- $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, according to the invertible matrix theorem, \n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A).$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)<n.$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$*  $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "783726e9-50d8-51db-9087-ab91d8cbf406" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358592} {:answer/id #uuid "358c1d14-b0e0-57f0-9f96-bfa81459e03c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358593} {:answer/id #uuid "802586e0-0294-5427-a504-6a0f9ce8f9d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358594} {:answer/id #uuid "48660cea-69f4-55ab-a3e8-7d3ee6ceebfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358595} {:answer/id #uuid "3d7e387a-3453-5174-b0a8-c07eaf25ae9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "802586e0-0294-5427-a504-6a0f9ce8f9d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358594} :answer-field/id #uuid "cae0a2de-ea19-5fbc-a007-4631181ce11f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c082f694-cfbd-5a5c-b403-d6ba66f9c740" :question/math-academy-id "q-142476" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{__________}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n- $det(A)=0$\n- $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}$\n- $A$ has $8$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $8\\times 8$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=8=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $  \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}.$*  $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $8$ pivot columns.* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=8,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $8$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358597 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d1700d2-29ed-53bf-8abc-bfc124bf80cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358599} {:answer/id #uuid "8e140777-add1-5998-b9fa-b0414f93a4c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358600} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e119a2-0cac-55bc-ac7a-387d109f79c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358601} {:answer/id #uuid "06d54aeb-55fd-5c43-9f47-3481e9250e4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358602} {:answer/id #uuid "d24ed2cc-152e-551a-8380-86e1c3f5f66a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4e119a2-0cac-55bc-ac7a-387d109f79c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358601} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a3d7f2-e626-5757-afd7-18d09f6e81f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358598}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5daba774-1192-5cc4-aee6-c7cca2d238bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-35425" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$  is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\n- $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$\n- $A$ is invertible\n- $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358604 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0812ec66-ff7b-59d5-9bba-542cbf206398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358606} {:answer/id #uuid "d0dfadcf-6b30-5082-985a-6ac7796ba43e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358607} {:answer/id #uuid "fb763252-8732-5c80-a9b8-dd124993793e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358608} {:answer/id #uuid "931da268-46aa-5027-a613-faeebb498d3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358609} {:answer/id #uuid "95b332ff-260f-512a-ad9e-ed0c0e113983" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0dfadcf-6b30-5082-985a-6ac7796ba43e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358607} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebcfa253-7e4f-567f-a5ea-73a04f6b3036" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e6dddf4-d251-52f4-b350-7dc4454f3ca2" :question/math-academy-id "q-47587" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n- $A$ has no inverse\n- $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n- All columns of $A$ are pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed,  a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$*$\\,\\times $\n\nSince our matrix is not invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, it must be $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.*  $\\,\\times $\n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n$, it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))<n,$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb499f85-bc50-5330-84da-3dbf03f8f6e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123527} {:answer/id #uuid "11e014c7-fa9b-5761-8312-d3df2870f8ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123528} {:answer/id #uuid "1ecc6b01-a08a-5008-8ae2-e0b6bc1da0e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123529} {:answer/id #uuid "34c8d9c8-001c-5de2-94d2-056b747df4b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123530} {:answer/id #uuid "482d56f8-dca9-512f-8238-7a60e4045329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11e014c7-fa9b-5761-8312-d3df2870f8ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123528} :answer-field/id #uuid "42a1c7fd-d593-542d-877c-2e51b07b0213" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f4e1182-d195-5cca-bb1a-601ea1f9c921" :question/math-academy-id "q-47599" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{__________}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n- $det(A)=0$\n- $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}$\n- $A$ has $5$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=7=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $5$ pivot columns.* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=7,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $7$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b73da8f-593d-59d7-b290-89ab874a96e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358613} {:answer/id #uuid "f448c6c2-f573-5946-bb8f-22f13bf108e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358614} {:answer/id #uuid "29996c6a-39ce-5ad1-b10b-470b9d105950" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358615} {:answer/id #uuid "8800b2e1-f98d-5195-9476-8aa846c51828" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358616} {:answer/id #uuid "bf274e47-eb66-592a-8286-3d59b18f2005" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b73da8f-593d-59d7-b290-89ab874a96e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358613} :answer-field/id #uuid "e05390a7-764a-52e6-88b2-45c77ecf26a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "34db7bbd-ba09-5ac3-b2e8-08dcdc73466b" :question/math-academy-id "q-79334" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n- $A$ is **not** invertible\n- $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n- $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is **not** invertible.* $\\,\\times $\n\nBy the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}]}
